WEBVTT

00:06.650 --> 00:08.240
Are they gone?

00:08.860 --> 00:10.860
The reporter left, too.

00:11.260 --> 00:14.820
Well, covering us has to be the 
least of her worries today.

00:15.750 --> 00:18.200
Listen. Drop this story.

00:18.200 --> 00:20.140
Wh-Why?!

00:20.140 --> 00:24.920
That building's been cropping up 
in all kinds of rumors for decades.

00:25.420 --> 00:29.790
Five years ago, blood from a high-ranking 
cop who went missing turned up there.

00:29.790 --> 00:33.140
Now a mugger hides in it, 
and they force a search?

00:33.140 --> 00:34.590
That's not normal.

00:35.000 --> 00:37.530
This is no job for a cub reporter.

00:37.530 --> 00:39.790
Hand it off to a veteran like Himura.

00:40.940 --> 00:43.730
No, this is my story.

00:45.350 --> 00:49.820
<i>If I force her to drop it, she'll take 
paid vacation and investigate anyway.</i>

00:50.250 --> 00:51.850
<i>I did it, Chief!</i>

00:51.850 --> 00:53.320
<i>I cracked the case, Chief!</i>

00:53.570 --> 00:55.200
<i>I've got photos to prove it, Chief!</i>

00:55.850 --> 00:59.450
<i>Still, it'd be a waste to fire her.</i>

01:01.210 --> 01:04.040
Fine. We'll compromise.

01:04.040 --> 01:09.250
You can cover the occult story on 
this fortune teller, the Corpse God.

01:09.460 --> 01:13.020
But don't take the initiative 
to go after anything else,

01:13.350 --> 01:15.380
and don't report on anything 
but fortune telling.

01:15.380 --> 01:16.570
Aww...

01:16.570 --> 01:18.140
Don't look at me like that.

01:18.410 --> 01:23.100
The flip side is that, if anything 
happens, you'll be closest to the scoop.

01:23.100 --> 01:24.970
I know, but...

01:24.970 --> 01:26.480
But what?

01:26.480 --> 01:31.360
Don't you trust your instinct that 
Polka Shinoyama's at the heart of this?

01:35.770 --> 01:38.490
You ought to know me better than that, Chief!

01:38.490 --> 01:43.370
I'll make Polka Shinoyama the 
center of this story, all right!

01:43.370 --> 01:44.750
Just watch me!

01:44.750 --> 01:48.350
Hey! Whatever else you do,
 don't lie in print!

03:19.960 --> 03:21.780
Excuse me, miss.

03:21.780 --> 03:24.530
I bought the extra things you asked me to.

03:25.010 --> 03:26.470
Thanks.

03:29.370 --> 03:32.170
So, seriously, what is that stuff?

03:33.100 --> 03:35.130
Well, think of it as a rent payment.

03:35.130 --> 03:36.210
Mana stones!

03:36.210 --> 03:37.840
Uncut gemstones?!

03:36.210 --> 03:38.190
<b>Mana Stone 

- Stones charged with magical power

 - Known in this world as gemstones</b>

03:36.210 --> 03:38.190
m 0 0 l 230 0 230 90 0 90

03:38.470 --> 03:42.660
I had Xiaoyu-kun visit a bunch 
of stores and buy them up for me.

03:43.400 --> 03:44.700
Are you sure about this?

03:44.700 --> 03:45.620
It's no big deal.

03:45.910 --> 03:49.080
After all, you saved the real Polka.

03:50.150 --> 03:52.750
<i>Miss Sayo knows that Polka is a fake, too?!</i>

03:53.200 --> 03:56.670
<i>What does she mean, 
he "saved the real Polka"?</i>

03:56.670 --> 03:59.800
<i>And what is he going to use that 
pile of rough gemstones for?</i>

03:59.800 --> 04:03.040
So, what can you do with all these?

04:03.040 --> 04:04.230
Good question.

04:04.230 --> 04:07.080
I think I could pull off one big task,

04:07.480 --> 04:10.540
but I already have a use in mind

04:10.540 --> 04:11.180
and that's...

04:13.040 --> 04:14.440
<i>What does he mean?</i>

04:15.210 --> 04:18.400
Now, the question is, what will we do next?

04:18.740 --> 04:23.280
I got in touch with Clarissa, but what 
about the dead body in that tunnel?

04:23.540 --> 04:24.240
<i>A dead body?!</i>

04:24.630 --> 04:25.920
<i>What are they talking about?!</i>

04:25.920 --> 04:29.200
For now, I'll make sure no one finds it.

04:29.200 --> 04:33.410
The dead guy is probably Nishida, 
one of Clarissa's bartenders.

04:33.730 --> 04:37.620
I sent Urai back to her in 
the confusion, but still.

04:37.620 --> 04:40.550
That guy worked at Clarissa's bar?

04:40.940 --> 04:44.220
The cops showed up right after 
someone dumped Nishida's body.

04:44.220 --> 04:48.680
That's gotta mean that the cops 
are working with the killer.

04:49.340 --> 04:49.970
Huh?

04:50.270 --> 04:51.590
Oh, crap!

04:51.590 --> 04:52.940
We'll finish this some other time!

04:52.940 --> 04:55.070
I'll slip out the back, 
so you take it from here!

04:55.070 --> 04:57.010
Call me if there's news!

04:57.010 --> 04:57.750
Bye!

04:58.440 --> 04:59.900
Uh... Okay.

05:04.910 --> 05:07.050
Wow! Looks tasty!

05:07.050 --> 05:09.570
I can never get over what 
a good cook you are.

05:09.570 --> 05:11.240
It's part of my job.

05:11.550 --> 05:13.860
Thanks for making this!

05:15.370 --> 05:16.070
Hi!

05:16.500 --> 05:17.620
Hello.

05:17.620 --> 05:20.360
Sorry. Were you in the middle of dinner?

05:20.360 --> 05:23.460
Did you come looking for that 
mugger, too, detectives?

05:23.460 --> 05:27.050
Nah. Unfortunately, 
we're on the Solitaire case.

05:27.490 --> 05:30.640
So, I'll cut to the chase.

05:32.130 --> 05:36.020
You already know why Solitaire 
came here, don't you?

05:38.110 --> 05:40.540
<i>Why Solitaire came here?</i>

05:41.330 --> 05:44.900
<i>This police officer shouldn't 
know about that symbol.</i>

05:45.300 --> 05:48.110
No, I have no idea.

05:48.470 --> 05:49.210
<i>Huh?!</i>

05:49.570 --> 05:53.950
<i>P-Polka, you know how I drew 
something for this detective?</i>

05:53.950 --> 05:54.660
<i>That was actually...</i>

05:55.760 --> 05:59.380
As far as I know, only one 
thing links you and Solitaire:

05:59.960 --> 06:02.340
the symbol painted on those blimps.

06:02.950 --> 06:06.050
You're in contact, aren't you? Come on.

06:06.650 --> 06:10.010
Won't you let me see Hosorogi-san?

06:12.800 --> 06:17.630
You mean you've been suspicious 
of my fortune telling all along?

06:18.140 --> 06:23.100
If you don't believe me, 
if we can't establish mutual trust,

06:23.100 --> 06:24.500
then I have nothing to say to—

06:24.500 --> 06:25.130
Hey.

06:26.150 --> 06:28.820
You can't brush me off this late in the game.

06:30.690 --> 06:31.690
<i>I can tell</i>

06:32.020 --> 06:36.230
<i>that danger is closing in,
 slowly but steadily.</i>

06:37.660 --> 06:40.020
<i>How far can my hands reach?</i>

06:40.480 --> 06:43.380
<i>Some souls may slip through my fingers.</i>

06:44.040 --> 06:45.840
<i>All the more reason to be careful.</i>

06:45.840 --> 06:48.800
Let's be honest with each other, kid.

06:48.800 --> 06:50.030
<i>Dinner...</i>

06:48.800 --> 06:50.760
<b>Dinner...</b>

06:50.760 --> 06:51.900
Can you prove

06:51.900 --> 06:55.820
that you haven't been drawn to 
the dark side of the police?

06:57.130 --> 07:00.060
"The answer lies in the 
paper that once guided you."

07:00.650 --> 07:04.020
"If you still believe in yourself,
 go on chasing it."

07:04.590 --> 07:07.630
Or so the person you're waiting for says.

07:13.180 --> 07:14.280
Ugh.

07:14.280 --> 07:16.870
Way too much happened today.

07:16.870 --> 07:19.280
For now, I'd better get all my info in order.

07:20.490 --> 07:21.170
Huh?

07:21.680 --> 07:24.380
I don't remember ordering anything.

07:24.590 --> 07:26.880
It couldn't be Arase... could it?

07:27.750 --> 07:30.220
H-Higuro-san?

07:30.770 --> 07:33.310
Why now, of all times?

07:34.090 --> 07:36.820
I wonder.

07:36.820 --> 07:38.310
Won't you come out?

07:38.980 --> 07:43.480
Higuro-san is so lonely, he might cry.

07:43.940 --> 07:48.610
Of course, you might end 
up crying a whole lot more.

07:47.770 --> 07:48.610
<b>Unlock</b>

07:49.540 --> 07:52.700
<i>Sit tight. I'll be right there.</i>

07:53.480 --> 07:57.480
So, Polka Shinoyama really is in 
contact with Inspector Hosorogi?

07:57.480 --> 07:58.930
Who knows?

07:58.930 --> 08:01.970
But either way, he's right.

08:01.970 --> 08:06.330
Following the lead on that 
fortune-telling paper comes first.

08:06.330 --> 08:08.130
Why not act now?

08:08.130 --> 08:13.010
I'd love to, but our plans will 
leak if we do anything careless.

08:13.010 --> 08:16.760
Nothing's easy when we can't 
trust our own organization, huh?

08:17.160 --> 08:18.490
You said it.

08:18.890 --> 08:22.270
No wonder Hosorogi-san
decided to disappear.

08:22.270 --> 08:25.270
<i>Corruption is eating away from the top.
 Don't trust anyone. 
There's another garage on the
 west side of that place.
 The signpost is inside. 
The key is behind the mirror of I-383.</i>

08:22.270 --> 08:25.270
m 0 0 l 280 0 280 190 0 190

08:23.230 --> 08:24.550
Oh, damn it.

08:25.760 --> 08:27.730
Looks like more rain.

08:30.230 --> 08:31.740
Long time, no see.

08:31.740 --> 08:33.650
What do you want <i>this</i> time?

08:34.900 --> 08:36.620
You don't like me much, I see.

08:36.620 --> 08:38.280
Of course not!

08:38.280 --> 08:42.130
You've gotta know I work for Clarissa now!

08:42.130 --> 08:43.540
I know.

08:44.170 --> 08:46.380
That's why I'm here.

08:48.090 --> 08:49.340
Figured it out?

08:49.770 --> 08:52.290
You're the one who made Nishida a mugger?

08:55.130 --> 08:59.120
Just now, you paused for a 
moment to think, didn't you?

09:00.290 --> 09:02.140
And to choose your words.

09:02.430 --> 09:07.230
You were wondering whether 
to say "mugger" or "corpse."

09:08.170 --> 09:10.270
It <i>was</i> you!

09:10.600 --> 09:13.140
You knew about the body.

09:13.140 --> 09:16.740
Pain is good. It slows judgment.

09:17.050 --> 09:21.200
Makes people fall for leading questions 
that would never normally catch them.

09:21.510 --> 09:26.070
Especially people who fear pain, like you.

09:26.560 --> 09:29.210
How did you hide the body in that situation?

09:30.020 --> 09:33.640
You see, my employer wants 
to use official power

09:33.640 --> 09:36.050
to lay everyone involved 
with your building bare,

09:36.750 --> 09:40.470
so I really need a mugger's 
corpse to turn up in it.

09:40.690 --> 09:43.220
You sure you oughta blab all that?

09:43.220 --> 09:46.760
Of course. A smart guy like you must realize

09:46.760 --> 09:49.690
that you have no choice now 
that you've heard my plans.

09:51.410 --> 09:52.570
Higuro-san.

09:53.230 --> 09:55.690
He might still have options.

10:03.240 --> 10:04.890
Misaki?

10:06.030 --> 10:08.000
Oh? Where's Misaki-chan?

10:08.300 --> 10:10.130
She went to pick up Takumi-kun.

10:10.510 --> 10:12.710
Clarissa-san called her about it.

10:13.160 --> 10:17.680
So, Shinjuku's intermediary 
predicted what I'd do.

10:25.770 --> 10:27.900
Are you using some kind of trick?

10:27.900 --> 10:30.900
No one your size should 
be able to overpower me.

10:32.000 --> 10:33.940
I'm a growing girl!

10:43.700 --> 10:45.620
Missed by a hair.

10:53.720 --> 10:57.080
No one's ever jumped over me before.

10:59.770 --> 11:01.650
In all honesty,

11:02.300 --> 11:04.300
that was a close one.

11:04.630 --> 11:06.460
Misaki. Hey.

11:06.460 --> 11:08.770
Misa... ki...

11:09.030 --> 11:13.520
Oh, dear. This could start a feud 
between Shibuya and Shinjuku.

11:13.520 --> 11:14.760
Sounds fun.

11:14.760 --> 11:18.780
If it means I get to fight a lot 
more like her, I'm all for it.

11:19.040 --> 11:20.790
I think I'll pass.

11:22.190 --> 11:25.010
Yes. Please forgive me.

11:25.010 --> 11:29.410
There was a slight irregularity. 
I'll give you a report later.

11:30.050 --> 11:33.610
Under Sabaramond's aegis, 
failure is impossible.

11:34.700 --> 11:38.170
Hey, are you sure that was the 
best thing to do with those gems?

11:38.170 --> 11:41.990
Yes. I can only do so much, after all.

11:42.860 --> 11:45.760
I'd already decided to use 
the first stones I got

11:46.230 --> 11:49.390
on Misaki-chan's evolution.

11:49.940 --> 11:52.850
I don't just want to extend 
the reach of my protection.

11:53.210 --> 11:56.120
I want to make more allies who 
can protect people with me.

11:57.140 --> 12:00.360
Misaki-chan isn't a zombie anymore.

12:01.260 --> 12:03.200
She's a vampire larva.

12:03.710 --> 12:05.540
What do you know?

12:05.540 --> 12:08.920
I got killed, but I didn't die. 
What a weird feeling.

12:08.920 --> 12:11.930
But maybe now I finally get

12:11.930 --> 12:14.370
how it feels to be a whole new me.

12:18.670 --> 12:21.550
Nope. I haven't changed.

12:28.890 --> 12:33.380
I've always been inhuman.

12:39.500 --> 12:41.780
<b>10 Years Ago</b>

12:40.560 --> 12:41.780
You...

12:41.780 --> 12:43.130
don't smile, do you?

12:45.930 --> 12:48.220
You'd look lovely if you did.

12:48.430 --> 12:53.180
I want to smile, but I forgot how.

12:53.180 --> 12:57.130
Well, everyone smiles for different reasons,

12:57.670 --> 13:01.680
but why don't you try doing something 
that someone else seems to like?

13:01.680 --> 13:02.590
Any ideas?

13:03.390 --> 13:06.430
Something that someone else seems to like?

13:08.340 --> 13:09.350
I know.

13:09.350 --> 13:11.910
What is it? I'll help you try it.

13:14.320 --> 13:15.770
Killing people.

13:22.100 --> 13:23.590
Something just hitched a ride.

13:23.590 --> 13:25.030
A pursuer, do you think?

13:29.860 --> 13:31.450
Whoops.

13:33.050 --> 13:34.090
They're gone.

13:34.990 --> 13:37.690
But I can catch up in no—

13:40.670 --> 13:41.880
Huh?

13:41.880 --> 13:43.210
Wow!

13:43.210 --> 13:47.120
I guess flying up is harder!

13:48.410 --> 13:50.850
Oh, found 'em!

13:57.300 --> 13:59.200
Whoa! Close call!

13:59.200 --> 14:02.820
But wow! This is amazing, Polka-kun!

14:02.820 --> 14:07.200
This body does just what I want, 
even though it's all new to me!

14:08.950 --> 14:12.620
Being a vampire rules! I love it!

14:13.110 --> 14:15.110
Hey, Clarissa,

14:15.110 --> 14:16.830
I'm having a ball right now!

14:17.510 --> 14:21.290
I found something fun 
apart from killing people!

14:22.040 --> 14:26.380
Who knew going to rescue 
someone would be so exciting?!

14:26.920 --> 14:29.780
Or that taking on someone 
way stronger than me

14:30.230 --> 14:32.930
could give me such a thrill?!

14:33.710 --> 14:36.600
I know you're awake, Takumi-kun.

14:37.440 --> 14:41.720
If you really are asleep, I could 
peel the skin off your arms to wake you.

14:41.720 --> 14:43.420
Fine!

14:43.420 --> 14:45.480
I'm awake! Just lay off the pain!

14:45.480 --> 14:50.450
Oh, good. I didn't want to lose 
face in front of Agakura-san.

14:50.710 --> 14:53.910
That beanpole's an Agakura?!

14:53.910 --> 14:57.520
"Beanpole"? Talk about retro vocabulary.

14:57.980 --> 15:01.610
Although I <i>am</i> the tallest in my family.

15:01.980 --> 15:06.000
Still, I guess we're pretty famous.

15:06.000 --> 15:07.750
Of course you are.

15:07.750 --> 15:12.140
The whole underworld knows the Agakuras 
are a family of elite nutjobs.

15:12.140 --> 15:17.290
"Never mess with that cult-like Crazy 
Bones Kagura gang or the Agakura family."

15:17.770 --> 15:19.450
You're the one who taught me that,

15:19.450 --> 15:20.600
Higuro-san.

15:20.600 --> 15:22.810
Yes, exactly.

15:23.230 --> 15:27.280
That's why I paid to get 
Agakura-san's family on my side.

15:27.730 --> 15:30.740
Just like you've allied with the Heilei.

15:31.910 --> 15:32.950
The who?

15:33.240 --> 15:35.320
You don't <i>look</i> like you're playing dumb.

15:35.920 --> 15:39.450
The Shinoyamas must not trust you completely.

15:39.450 --> 15:41.250
What do you mean?

15:41.500 --> 15:44.710
You know that black-haired 
boy in your building?

15:44.970 --> 15:47.420
He's an assassin on the 
Shinoyama family's payroll.

15:49.090 --> 15:52.140
I was hoping to plant a listening 
device at Takumi's place

15:52.140 --> 15:54.970
and learn more about that "dead body."

15:55.920 --> 15:58.560
But why... why is one of them<i> here?</i>

15:59.610 --> 16:00.620
An Agakura!

16:04.920 --> 16:07.190
I guess the Agakuras are off-limits.

16:07.930 --> 16:08.780
No.

16:09.230 --> 16:11.360
I'm not a Heilei anymore.

16:11.580 --> 16:16.530
It wouldn't hurt to rescue that guy 
and put the fake Polka in my debt.

16:16.850 --> 16:20.220
Now, let's continue our chat.

16:20.220 --> 16:23.680
You have no choice. I got that far, didn't I?

16:23.680 --> 16:24.580
Hey.

16:25.040 --> 16:27.940
Doesn't he have two? Choices, I mean.

16:27.940 --> 16:30.210
Cooperate or die.

16:30.210 --> 16:32.490
Oh, not in his case.

16:32.800 --> 16:34.050
Right, Takumi-kun?

16:34.780 --> 16:39.390
To avoid imminent death, you'll sacrifice 
the present without a second thought.

16:39.600 --> 16:42.270
This thing on your head is proof of that.

16:42.860 --> 16:45.590
As a child, you believed 
in the good in people,

16:45.250 --> 16:48.440
Dad

16:45.250 --> 16:48.440
It's your fault.

16:45.590 --> 16:48.440
but society and your parents 
betrayed you spectacularly.

16:47.250 --> 16:48.440
Family Suicide

16:48.900 --> 16:55.510
Then you believed that evil was the way to go,
so you joined the Sanzu Sons...

16:55.510 --> 16:58.910
only for Arase to crush the 
gang and your convictions.

16:59.480 --> 17:02.450
Good and evil don't feel real to you.

17:02.450 --> 17:03.640
I heard

17:04.710 --> 17:07.720
that you've developed a phobia of reality.

17:08.490 --> 17:13.940
For peace of mind, you pretend everything 
you see through your cameras is a game.

17:14.330 --> 17:17.300
How courageous. I could cry.

17:17.590 --> 17:19.760
You seem to know a lot about me.

17:20.060 --> 17:23.390
Because I valued your ability 
to gather intelligence.

17:23.390 --> 17:26.750
I would have liked to recruit 
you again if I got the chance,

17:26.750 --> 17:29.810
but Kuraki-san seems to have 
taken quite a liking to you.

17:30.190 --> 17:33.320
What were you doing in 
that infamous building?

17:33.790 --> 17:37.530
I'd appreciate it if you'd 
tell me that and so much more.

17:38.180 --> 17:40.720
You don't want to get a 
game over yet, do you?

17:43.790 --> 17:46.080
I really can't reach his phone.

17:43.790 --> 17:46.080
<b>Recent Calls</b>

17:43.790 --> 17:46.080
