17:46.080 --> 17:48.150
I've been wondering for a while now.

17:48.150 --> 17:51.020
Can we even trust that guy?

17:51.020 --> 17:53.880
He'll obey as long as we leash him with fear,

17:53.880 --> 17:58.430
but I can't guarantee his loyalty if 
something scares him more than we do.

17:58.430 --> 18:01.330
So, he's a lost cause if 
our enemies catch him?

18:01.330 --> 18:04.130
We should have rigged him to self-destruct.

18:05.410 --> 18:06.490
You have a point.

18:06.490 --> 18:08.500
That's what made this a perfect fit.

18:09.270 --> 18:12.980
He needed a shackle other than fear.

18:13.200 --> 18:16.950
A new connection, different from us.

18:18.300 --> 18:20.240
I'm stumped.

18:20.240 --> 18:23.030
Sure, I'm scared of a game over,

18:23.030 --> 18:27.290
but wouldn't giving in to you 
now be a bad ending, too?

18:28.750 --> 18:32.000
Don't worry. I only grazed you.

18:32.000 --> 18:37.150
Most movies treat being shot in 
the arm or leg as a minor injury,

18:37.470 --> 18:41.470
but in the real world, you'll bleed 
out if the shot hits a major artery.

18:41.750 --> 18:45.750
Besides, you're going to 
talk in the end, anyway.

18:46.950 --> 18:51.190
No secret is worth more to 
you than your life, is it?

18:51.650 --> 18:56.320
I've got no secrets worth 
more than a friend's life.

19:00.160 --> 19:03.480
Yeah. That's right.

19:04.270 --> 19:05.740
Higuro-san.

19:05.740 --> 19:07.620
Do you feel like answering now?

19:08.720 --> 19:13.840
No one likes a guy who nitpicks 
unrealistic stuff in movies.

19:14.070 --> 19:16.000
Oh, I second that.

19:17.540 --> 19:19.170
Do you think I'm bluffing?

19:20.130 --> 19:22.470
<i>Something feels... off.</i>

19:23.130 --> 19:28.680
<i>Like he's afraid of pain,
 but not actually afraid of dying.</i>

19:29.410 --> 19:30.640
<i>If I die,</i>

19:31.330 --> 19:33.600
<i>salvage my life, too, Polka!</i>

19:36.510 --> 19:38.970
You know, I had shumai for lunch.

19:39.840 --> 19:42.200
I only eat them with mustard.

19:42.550 --> 19:43.470
<b>Soy Sauce</b>

19:46.990 --> 19:48.530
Do you feel more talkative now?

19:49.960 --> 19:51.260
I want...

19:52.660 --> 19:54.890
to dig my heels in a little, too.

19:55.510 --> 19:57.920
'Cause if I don't,

19:58.520 --> 20:01.130
I'll never get anywhere.

20:01.400 --> 20:05.430
I wish you'd been this stubborn 
when Arase threatened you.

20:06.800 --> 20:08.880
Just so you know,

20:08.880 --> 20:11.230
I could do this just as 
well with someone else.

20:13.520 --> 20:14.630
For example,

20:14.630 --> 20:17.850
that girl hugging the plush shark.

20:19.100 --> 20:22.370
Hold on. Do you know who she is?

20:22.370 --> 20:25.700
You'd turn the Shinoyamas against you.

20:25.700 --> 20:27.580
Oh, don't worry about that.

20:27.580 --> 20:29.510
The higher-ups will step in for me.

20:29.970 --> 20:31.140
"Higher-ups"?

20:31.140 --> 20:33.830
So rest easy and writhe on the ground.

20:34.380 --> 20:36.400
Even if you happen to die,

20:36.750 --> 20:39.090
I have replacements all lined up.

20:42.530 --> 20:44.590
I found a reason to save him.

20:45.130 --> 20:48.320
If Miss Sayo is next on 
your list when he dies,

20:48.320 --> 20:51.270
I'd better keep him alive as a decoy.

20:51.530 --> 20:52.560
Oh?

20:53.210 --> 20:55.370
And I found a reason to kill you.

20:55.700 --> 20:58.270
If you're out to hurt the Shinoyamas,

20:58.560 --> 21:01.110
that makes you my enemies!

21:02.060 --> 21:04.570
A mugging in Shinjuku?

21:04.570 --> 21:08.700
Yes. They searched that building where 
Solitaire appeared for the culprit.

21:08.700 --> 21:11.240
Hang on. That's not—

21:12.090 --> 21:16.050
No, wait. The building 
where Solitaire appeared.

21:16.050 --> 21:16.750
Isn't that

21:17.480 --> 21:18.720
where Hosorogi's...?

21:20.460 --> 21:25.820
I'll look into it. But remember, 
don't get emotional.

21:25.820 --> 21:29.730
I can't cover for you 
if you go off the rails.

21:29.730 --> 21:31.330
I'll be fine, sir.

21:31.330 --> 21:34.480
I have subordinates to stop me now, 
and they'd punch me out to do it.

21:37.270 --> 21:38.640
Enter.

21:51.490 --> 21:53.190
A fine chair.

21:54.130 --> 21:57.750
I daresay it's fit to bear the 
weight of your responsibilities.

21:58.210 --> 22:01.450
If you want to turn yourself in, 
you've come to the wrong place,

22:01.870 --> 22:03.510
Phantom Solitaire.
